# User changelog

`VikingChangelog.md` (repository root) is installed beside Viking.exe. Viking shows it from **Help > Change Log** and once
the first time each version starts, so it is written for the people who use Viking.

- A commit that changes what a Viking user can see or do (behaviour, a fix they could notice, a hotkey, menu, dialog,
  preference or default) adds a bullet to the newest section of `VikingChangelog.md` in the same commit.
- One `## <version> — <date, or "not yet released">` heading per version, newest first, each followed by a bulleted list.
  The newest heading is the version in `Clients/Viking/Viking/Viking.csproj` (`ChangelogTests` in `VikingCoreTests` checks
  this): when that version changes, rename the unreleased heading. When a version ships, replace "not yet released" with
  the date and channel, for example `2026-10-26 (Viking Test, unsigned)`.
- Write bullets for users: what changed and how to use it, naming menus, buttons, hotkeys and preferences as Viking shows
  them. Leave out internal refactors and build changes. Notes only developers need go in an HTML comment (`<!-- -->`),
  which Viking does not show.
- Start each bullet with a bold summary of 2–7 plain words that lets a reader skim (a fix keeps `Fix:` inside the bold),
  then the full detail as plain text that does not repeat the summary, for example
  `* **Fix: Capture Screen when zoomed in.** **Capture Screen** (Commands menu) showed an error instead of its dialog …`.
- Supported Markdown: `#` headings, `*` or `-` bullets (indent two spaces to nest), paragraphs, `**bold**`, `` `code` `` and
  `[text](https://…)` links. Links into the repository are shown as plain text.
